1. `ps aux | grep "codex exec" | grep -v grep` — which still run? (42254=r135 RESUMED connection logging fixes, code + local tests only, NO adb; 35418=r136 RESUMED C2+H A/B on BOARD — allowed: swap prompt/progressive-tools/device-mcp configs with .pre-r136 backups, restart device-mcp + middleware-service only).
2. For each running one: log /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-edgeAgent/2acae017-2470-4056-ac60-2e0590d533bc/scratchpad/{r135b-codex.log,r136b-codex.log} and rollout ~/.codex/sessions/2026/10/13/*<session id>*.jsonl (r135 01a133d0-2a5f-7b73-b0ee-73c0824b2375, r136 01a133d7-c01a-7820-aaae-24fe6b16f161): mtime + last ~15 log lines. Not changed for more than 25 minutes, or repeating the same error, counts as stalled. For r136: done.txt in docs/proposals/evidence/c2h-enable-r136-20261013/ growing past 12.
